.TH SHARDPOSTCTL-TRACE 1 "2026-09-20" "ShardPost 0.26.1" "ShardPost Manual"
.SH NAME
shardpostctl-trace \- record the IMAP protocol of one account for a while
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shardpostctl trace on
.RB [ \-for
.IR duration ]
.I account
.br
.B shardpostctl trace status
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I account
.br
.B shardpostctl trace off
.I account
.SH DESCRIPTION
Switches on a protocol trace for one account: every IMAP command and
response of its sessions is written to the server log as
.IR event=protocol_trace .
This is the tool for "it works with every client except this one".
.PP
The switch is stored with the account, so it applies on every server of
the cluster, no matter which one the client happens to reach. Sessions
that are already open pick it up within
.I trace.recheck_seconds
(60 by default), so you do not have to ask the user to reconnect.
.PP
A trace always expires on its own. Without
.B \-for
it runs for
.IR trace.default_duration_seconds ,
and no trace can outlast
.IR trace.max_duration_seconds .
.PP
Credentials never reach the log: a LOGIN or AUTHENTICATE command stops
the trace for that session, unlogged, until the next login, so neither
the password nor pipelined SASL data can appear. PREVIEW responses, which
quote message text, are masked.
.PP
Role:
.BR trace .
.SS trace status
Reports whether a trace is on and when it expires.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-for " duration"
How long the trace lasts, for example
.IR 30m ,
.IR 2h .
Only for
.BR "trace on" .
The server caps it at its maximum.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the status as JSON.
.SH EXAMPLES
A user's phone does not show new mail. Trace them for half an hour:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl trace on -for 30m user@example.org
shardpostctl trace status user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
Read what the client actually sent, on both servers:
.PP
.nf
.RS
for p in $(kubectl -n shardpost get pod \\
        -l app.kubernetes.io/name=shardpost-server -o name); do
    kubectl -n shardpost logs $p -c server --since=10m \\
        | grep protocol_trace | grep user@example.org
done
.RE
.fi
.PP
Switch it off as soon as you have what you need:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl trace off user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 64
The duration is not valid, or
.B \-for
was used with
.B off
or
.BR status .
.TP
.B 67
No such account.
.TP
.B 77
The caller lacks the role
.BR trace .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shardpostctl (1),
.BR shardpostctl-account (1)
.PP
The trace settings are described in
.IR docs/configuration.md .
